<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('../partials/head') %></head>
<body>
<div class="app">
<%- include('../partials/sidebar') %>
<%- include('../partials/topbar') %>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
      <p class="hint mt-0">
        <strong>What this report measures, and what it samples.</strong>
        Everything about a competitor's content — their inventory, their topics, their entities, their anchor
        text, their schema, their publishing rate, their AI-retrieval posture — is measured from a live fetch of
        their site. Referring domains are a <em>verified sample</em>: candidate pages are found by a keyless web
        search, then each one is fetched and its outbound links read, so every domain counted carries a real link
        — but the candidate list is capped, so the counts are floors rather than totals. Keyword positions are
        read from a keyless result page unless a rank-tracker credential is configured, and are labelled
        accordingly. Organic traffic estimates and actual AI citation share are not available at all and are not
        shown.
      </p>
      <p class="hint">
        <strong>The gap lists are filtered.</strong> A competitor's own brand name is structurally the entity
        most certain to appear on their pages and not on this one, so before filtering it topped every list and
        the report was advising the client to write about their rivals. Competitor brand names, generic button
        and section labels ("Learn More", "Why Choose Us", "Office Headquarters") and each site's own template
        text are now suppressed — and what was suppressed is listed on the result page, because a filter nobody
        can inspect is a filter nobody can trust.
      </p>

      <p class="hint" style="margin-bottom:0">
        <strong>What is still not available at all:</strong>
        <% if (notMeasured && notMeasured.length) { %>
          organic traffic estimates, and which pages AI assistants actually cite. Nothing is shown for either —
          a fabricated traffic figure is indistinguishable on screen from a real one. Referring domains and
          keyword positions <em>are</em> now produced, as the verified sample and the labelled non-Google
          comparison described above; configuring
          <%= notMeasured.map(function (p) { return p.label; }).join(', ') %>
          replaces the samples with complete counts and the sampled positions with live Google SERPs. The
          adapters exist — set the environment variables and they activate.
        <% } else { %>
          nothing — every configured provider is available, so every table on the result page uses measured data
          rather than a sample.
        <% } %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%- include('_partials/brandpicker') %>

  <% if (brand) { %>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-head"><h3>Competitors for <%= brand.name %></h3></div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <% if (!competitors.length) { %>
        <div class="empty-state">
          None yet. Name two to four domains you genuinely compete with — a list guessed from SERP overlap on a
          small keyword set is wrong often enough to waste the crawl it costs.
        </div>
      <% } else { %>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data">
          <thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Label</th><th>Active</th><th>Added</th><th></th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
          <% competitors.forEach(function (c) { %>
            <tr>
              <td><a href="https://<%= c.domain %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><%= c.domain %></a></td>
              <td class="muted"><%= c.label || '—' %></td>
              <td><%= c.active ? 'yes' : 'no' %></td>
              <td class="muted"><%= fmtDate(c.created_at) %></td>
              <td>
                <% if (perms.canWrite) { %>
                  <form method="POST" action="/ai-seo/competitors/<%= c.id %>/remove" class="inline-form">
                    <input type="hidden" name="brand_id" value="<%= brand.id %>">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn danger-ghost xs">Remove</button>
                  </form>
                <% } %>
              </td>
            </tr>
          <% }) %>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>
      <% } %>

      <form method="POST" action="/ai-seo/competitors/add" style="margin-top:14px">
        <input type="hidden" name="brand_id" value="<%= brand.id %>">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="domains">Add competitors <span class="muted">(one per line — optionally <code>domain.com | Their label</code>)</span></label>
          <textarea id="domains" name="domains" rows="3" placeholder="competitor-one.com | The incumbent&#10;competitor-two.com"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <button type="submit" class="btn secondary" <%= perms.canWrite ? '' : 'disabled' %>>Save competitors</button>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-head"><h3>Run the comparison</h3></div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <form method="POST" action="/ai-seo/competitors/run">
        <input type="hidden" name="brand_id" value="<%= brand.id %>">
        <div class="field-row">
          <label class="field">
            <span>Pages to crawl per site</span>
            <select name="max_pages">
              <option value="15">15 — quick</option>
              <option value="30" selected>30 — default</option>
              <option value="60">60</option>
              <option value="120">120 — slow, and it crawls every site</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Country <span class="muted">(for the keyword gap)</span></span>
            <select name="country">
              <% marketList.forEach(function (mk) { %>
                <option value="<%= mk.code %>" <%= mk.code === selectedMarket ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= mk.name %></option>
              <% }) %>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Keywords in the gap table</span>
            <select name="keyword_gap_limit">
              <option value="10">10 — fastest</option>
              <option value="25" selected>25</option>
              <option value="40">40</option>
              <option value="60">60 — slow</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Backlink sample per site</span>
            <select name="backlink_sample_limit">
              <option value="10">10 candidates</option>
              <option value="20" selected>20 candidates</option>
              <option value="35">35 candidates</option>
              <option value="50">50 candidates — slow</option>
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="checkbox-row">
          <label class="check">
            <input type="checkbox" name="include_matrix" checked>
            Build the topic coverage matrix
            <span class="muted">— one row per topic, one column per site, one score computed identically for everybody. Replaces the two flat gap lists, which said what was missing but not how far behind.</span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="checkbox-row">
          <label class="check">
            <input type="checkbox" name="include_keyword_gap" checked>
            Build the keyword gap table
            <span class="muted">— where each site appears for each candidate keyword. Measured against Google where a rank-tracker credential exists; otherwise read from a keyless result sample and labelled as not-Google on every row.</span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="checkbox-row">
          <label class="check">
            <input type="checkbox" name="include_backlink_gap" checked>
            Build the backlink gap table
            <span class="muted">— referring domains per site, and the domains linking to a competitor and not to this brand. Every candidate page is fetched and its outbound links read, so a domain only counts where a real link exists.</span>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="checkbox-row">
          <label class="check">
            <input type="checkbox" name="want_ai" <%= aiAvailable ? 'checked' : 'disabled' %>>
            Ask the model to prioritise the gaps and say which ones not to chase
            <% if (!aiAvailable) { %><span class="muted">— needs an Azure OpenAI credential</span><% } %>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="checkbox-row">
          <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="force" value="1"> Regenerate rather than reusing the cached prioritisation</label>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <button type="submit" class="btn" <%= perms.canWrite && competitors.filter(function(c){ return c.active; }).length ? '' : 'disabled' %>>
            Run comparison
          </button>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">
          This crawls this site plus up to five competitor sites, so with a 30-page budget it makes roughly
          180 requests and takes a few minutes. It runs in the background — the result page refreshes itself.
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
  <% } %>

  <%- include('_partials/runs') %>

<%- include('../partials/sidebar-end') %>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
